* NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design. Simulated results; models as stated; nothing has been built or measured.
* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
*
* Behavioural electro-thermal model of the Microchip MSC080SMA330B4N (3.3 kV, 80 mOhm SiC MOSFET).
* BUILT BY THIS PROJECT FROM THE DATASHEET, NOT THE MAKER'S MODEL. Microchip's SPICE download
* (microchip.com software library) returned HTTP 403 to automated retrieval on 2026-11-27.
* Datasheet used: DS00005914A (2025), copy from https://docs.rs-online.com/a067/A700000015733917.pdf,
* read 2026-11-27.
*
* Figures used and how:
*  - Channel: square law Id = K*(Vgs-Vt)^2 in saturation, level-1 linear region below it.
*    Fitted to Fig 1-2 (Tj 25 C, VDS 35 V): 6 V -> ~3 A, 8 V -> ~16 A, 10 V -> ~38 A, 12 V -> ~65 A,
*    14 V -> ~100 A  =>  K = 1.03 A/V^2, Vt = 4.06 V (extrapolated square-law threshold, not the 3 mA
*    VGS(th) of Table 1-3).  Fig 1-4 (150 C): 6 V -> ~13 A, 10 V -> ~65 A => Vt = 2.77 V.
*    Vt(T) = vt25 - 0.0103*(T-25) [linear between the two fits]. K held constant with temperature
*    (the 150 C fit gives a higher K, but mobility falls with T at high VGS; constant K is the
*    middle choice) [EST].
*  - Mobility degradation th (default 0): kp/(1+th*Vov). th=0 gives ~230 A at VGS 20 V in saturation;
*    th=0.06 gives ~170 A. Fig 1-2 is not saturated at 35 V for VGS >= 16 V, so the true value is
*    unknown; netlists run th=0 (more current, worse for shoot-through) and report th as a sensitivity.
*  - Channel-length modulation lam = 1e-4 /V (+22 % current at 2.2 kV) [ASSUMPTION: the datasheet gives
*    no saturation data above 35 V; SiC short-circuit currents at kV are known to exceed the low-VDS curves].
*  - RDS(on) 106 mOhm MAX at 20 V/25 C (Table 1-3) = channel (1/(2*K*16 V) = 30 mOhm) + rd25 76 mOhm.
*    Temperature factor of Fig 1-5: f(T) = 1 + 0.0072*(T-25) + 1.92e-5*(T-25)^2 (1.41 at 75, 2.2 at 150).
*  - Gate: internal ESR 3.7 Ohm (Table 1-4); Cgs = Ciss - Crss = 3.46 nF; Cgd = 2.02 nF/(1+V)^0.8, i.e.
*    4 pF at 2.4 kV (Crss) and ~49 nC from 0 to 2.65 kV (QGD 51 nC, Table 1-4); 1.2 nF at 1 V.
*    (modelled as the capacitance of a junction that never conducts).
*  - Coss: body-diode junction capacitance CJO 3.1 nF, VJ 1 V, M 0.5 -> 64 pF at 2.4 kV, ~300 nC at
*    2.4 kV (Fig 1-7/1-8, +/-20 %).
*  - Body diode: IS 1e-15, N 3.4, RS 25 mOhm -> 4.1 V at 30 A (Table 1-5: 4.2 V typ at VGS -5 V).
*    Reverse recovery not modelled (Qrr 818 nC is mostly capacitive in SiC).
*  - Thermal: Foster network fitted to the single-pulse Zth of Fig 1-18 as read in WP-G section 4
*    (0.016 C/W at 10 us ... 0.28 plateau) and EXTRAPOLATED below 10 us as sqrt(t)
*    (0.0051 at 1 us, 0.0016 at 0.1 us). The fit is within +/-1.5 % of those points. Case node held at
*    the parameter tc (starting junction temperature). Node tj carries the junction temperature in
*    volts = degrees C. The electrical parameters follow tj (electro-thermal).
*  - No avalanche, no short-circuit failure, no gate leakage, no turn-off SOA: the datasheet publishes
*    none of these, so the model cannot say when the part is destroyed. Judge results against Tj 150 C
*    (rating) and treat anything beyond it as "outside every published figure".
*
* Pins: d g s tj    (g = external gate pin; tj = thermal output node, leave it to a probe)
.subckt msc080b d g s tj params: tc=55 vt25=4.06 kp=1.03 lam=1e-4 rd25=0.0755 th=0
Rgi g gi 3.7
Cgs gi s 3.46n
* gate-drain capacitance as a never-conducting junction (IS 1e-30, N 50: < 1e-20 A at +20 V forward)
Dcgd gi d dcgd_msc
.model dcgd_msc d (is=1e-30 n=50 cjo=2.02n vj=1 m=0.8 fc=0.5)
* drain series resistance (temperature dependent)
Brd d di I = V(d,di) / ( rd25*(1 + 0.0072*(V(tj)-25) + 1.92e-5*(V(tj)-25)^2) )
* channel
Bch di s I = kp/(1+th*0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)))*(1+lam*abs(V(di,s))) * sgn(V(di,s)) *
+ ( abs(V(di,s)) < 0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)) ?
+   2*0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1))*abs(V(di,s)) - V(di,s)^2 :
+   (0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)))^2 )
* body diode with Coss as its junction capacitance; current measured by Vbd
Vbd s sb 0
Dbody sb di dbody_msc
.model dbody_msc d (is=1e-15 n=3.4 rs=0.025 cjo=3.1n vj=1 m=0.5 bv=4000)
* dissipated power into the thermal network
Bpwr 0 tj I = V(d,di)^2/( rd25*(1 + 0.0072*(V(tj)-25) + 1.92e-5*(V(tj)-25)^2) )
+ + V(di,s)*( kp/(1+th*0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)))*(1+lam*abs(V(di,s))) * sgn(V(di,s)) *
+ ( abs(V(di,s)) < 0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)) ?
+   2*0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1))*abs(V(di,s)) - V(di,s)^2 :
+   (0.1*ln(1+exp((V(gi,s)-(vt25-0.0103*(V(tj)-25)))/0.1)))^2 ) )
+ + abs(I(Vbd)*V(s,di))
* Foster network, tau / R from the fit (C = tau/R)
Vcase tcase 0 {tc}
R1 tj t1 0.00186
C1 tj t1 53.8u
R2 t1 t2 0.00067
C2 t1 t2 746u
R3 t2 t3 0.00329
C3 t2 t3 608u
R4 t3 t4 0.01060
C4 t3 t4 943u
R5 t4 t5 0.00934
C5 t4 t5 5.35m
R6 t5 t6 0.02161
C6 t5 t6 11.57m
R7 t6 t7 0.04678
C7 t6 t7 21.4m
R8 t7 t8 0.07920
C8 t7 t8 50.5m
R9 t8 tcase 0.10777
C9 t8 tcase 139m
.ends msc080b
